@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `law08-vintage`
IMPORT `law08-nouns`
IMPORT `law08-ch7-commencement`

-- Chuong III, Muc 6 (Dieu 94-108): capital, capital adequacy, deposit, technical reserves, reserve fund,
-- investment, separating equity from premium sources (Dieu 101, amended by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(8)),
-- financial year, audit, reports. Dieu 94(4)-(5), 95 and 99(3)-(4) do not take effect until 1 January 2028
-- (Dieu 156(2), both texts): a rule on them takes the day of the question and declines before that day.
-- Money is VND.

§ `Chuong III, Muc 6: Tai chinh, hach toan ke toan va bao cao tai chinh`

§§ `Dieu 94: capital`

@@q 1985 1988
@ref Dieu 94 (src:1985-1988)
`Dieu 94(1)-(2) — definitions of charter capital and of allocated capital of a foreign branch (the amounts are inputs of the record of the insurer's capital)` MEANS
    "Charter capital is the sum members paid or promised, or the par value of shares sold or registered; allocated capital is what the foreign parent gives the branch."

-- Dieu 94(3): owners' equity is the paid-up charter capital, the branch's allocated capital, reserve funds,
-- undistributed after-tax profit and the owner's funds set aside from after-tax profit.
@@q 1992 1994
@ref Dieu 94 (src:1992-1994)
GIVEN c IS A `The capital of an insurer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 94(3): the owners' equity` c MEANS
        c's `charter capital paid up`
    PLUS c's `capital allocated to a foreign branch`
    PLUS c's `reserve funds`
    PLUS c's `undistributed after-tax profit`
    PLUS c's `funds of the owner set aside from after-tax profit`

-- Dieu 94(4): available capital is owners' equity plus other sources the Ministry of Finance allows to be
-- recognised, less the deductions it requires. Takes effect on 1 January 2028 (Dieu 156(2)).
@@q 1995 1996
@ref Dieu 94 (src:1995-1996)
GIVEN c IS A `The capital of an insurer`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 94(4): the available capital on the day` c `the day in question` MEANS
    IF `Dieu 156(2): the provision is in force on the day` `Dieu 94(4) and (5)` `the day in question`
    THEN `Dieu 94(3): the owners' equity` c PLUS c's `other sources the Ministry of Finance allows to be recognised` MINUS c's `amounts the Ministry of Finance requires to be deducted`
    ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 94(4) and (5) are not yet in force on that day (Dieu 156(2)); the provision of the old Law that governs until then is not among the sources"

@@q 2013 2015
@ref Dieu 94 (src:2013-2015)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 94(6): the minimum charter capital or minimum allocated capital for the kind of insurer` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 94(6) delegates the minimum charter capital and minimum allocated capital to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 95: the capital adequacy ratio`

-- Dieu 95(1)-(3). The ratio is available capital over risk-based capital; the investment in other insurers,
-- other reinsurers and subsidiaries of insurers and reinsurers is not counted in available capital. The
-- minimum ratio is "not lower than prescribed" (Dieu 95(2); the Minister fixes it, Dieu 95(4)): an input.
@@q 2017 2026
@ref Dieu 95 (src:2017-2026)
GIVEN c IS A `The capital of an insurer`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 95(1): the capital adequacy ratio on the day` c `the day in question` MEANS
    IF NOT `Dieu 156(2): the provision is in force on the day` `Dieu 95` `the day in question`
    THEN REFUSE "Dieu 95 is not yet in force on that day (Dieu 156(2)); the provision of the old Law that governs until then is not among the sources"
    ELSE IF c's `risk-based capital` AT MOST 0
         THEN REFUSE "Dieu 95(1): the risk-based capital is not positive, so the ratio is undefined"
         ELSE (`Dieu 94(4): the available capital on the day` c `the day in question` MINUS c's `amount invested in other insurers, other reinsurers and subsidiaries of insurers and reinsurers`) DIVIDED BY c's `risk-based capital`

GIVEN c IS A `The capital of an insurer`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the minimum ratio the Minister of Finance prescribes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 95(2): the insurer keeps the ratio not below the prescribed ratio` c `the day in question` `the minimum ratio the Minister of Finance prescribes` MEANS
    `Dieu 95(1): the capital adequacy ratio on the day` c `the day in question` AT LEAST `the minimum ratio the Minister of Finance prescribes`

@@q 2025 2026
@ref Dieu 95 (src:2025-2026)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 95(4): the Minister of Finance's rules on the capital adequacy ratio, risk-based capital and available capital` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 95(4) delegates the detail of the capital adequacy ratio, the risk-based capital and the available capital to the Minister of Finance; the Minister's circular is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 96: the deposit`

-- Dieu 96(1)-(2). The deposit at a commercial bank is 2% of the minimum charter capital (or minimum allocated
-- capital) at the time of establishment. The minimum is the Government's (Dieu 94(6)): an input.
@@q 2028 2033
@ref Dieu 96 (src:2028-2033)
GIVEN d IS A `A deposit`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 96(2): the deposit the insurer must make` d MEANS
    d's `minimum charter capital or minimum allocated capital at the time of establishment` TIMES 2%

GIVEN d IS A `A deposit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 96(2): the deposit made is the amount the Law requires` d MEANS
    d's `amount deposited` EQUALS `Dieu 96(2): the deposit the insurer must make` d

-- Dieu 96(3). The deposit may be used only to meet commitments to policyholders when solvency is short, with the
-- Ministry's written approval, and must be made good within 90 days of the day it was used.
@@q 2036 2041
@ref Dieu 96 (src:2036-2041)
GIVEN d IS A `A deposit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 96(3): the use of the deposit is permitted` d MEANS
    d's `the deposit is used to meet commitments to policyholders because solvency is short` AND d's `the Ministry of Finance approved the use in writing`

GIVEN d IS A `A deposit`
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 96(3): the last day to replenish the deposit` d MEANS
    d's `date the deposit was used` PLUS 90

GIVEN d IS A `A deposit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 96(3): the deposit was replenished in time` d MEANS
    d's `date the deposit used was replenished` AT MOST `Dieu 96(3): the last day to replenish the deposit` d

@@q 2042 2043
@ref Dieu 96 (src:2042-2043)
GIVEN d IS A `A deposit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 96(4): the withdrawal of the whole deposit is permitted` d MEANS
    (NOT d's `the whole deposit is being withdrawn`) OR d's `the business has ceased`

§§ `Dieu 97: technical reserves`

@@q 2045 2065
@ref Dieu 97 (src:2045-2065)
GIVEN r IS A `A technical reserve`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 97(2)-(3): the technical reserve meets the requirements` r MEANS
        r's `set aside separately for each line of insurance`
    AND r's `corresponds to the liability committed under the contracts`
    AND r's `separate for contracts with objects inside and outside Vietnam, unless the law provides otherwise`
    AND r's `backed always by assets that correspond to it, with separate assets for the reserve for contracts abroad`
    AND r's `computed and set aside using the actuary`
    AND r's `reviewed and assessed regularly and made good in time`
    AND r's `the method of setting it aside was registered and approved by the Ministry of Finance`

@@q 2068 2069
@ref Dieu 97 (src:2068-2069)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 97(4): the Government's rules on setting aside technical reserves and on registering the method` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 97(4) delegates the detail to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 98: the reserve fund`

-- Dieu 98(1)-(2). The compulsory reserve fund is set aside each year at 5% of after-tax profit until it equals the
-- maximum the Government fixes. When the maximum is not supplied the contribution cannot be completed: the
-- Law gives no maximum. The contribution in the last year is read as no more than the room left (F24).
@@q 2071 2075
@ref Dieu 98 (src:2071-2075)
GIVEN f IS A `A reserve fund position`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 98(2): the contribution to the compulsory reserve fund for the year` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `maximum the Government fixes for the compulsory reserve fund`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "Dieu 98(2) sets aside 5% of after-tax profit until the fund equals a maximum the Government fixes; no maximum is supplied"
    WHEN JUST m THEN max 0 (min (f's `after-tax profit of the year` TIMES 5%) (m MINUS f's `balance of the compulsory reserve fund`))

§§ `Dieu 99: general rules on investment`

-- Dieu 99(2)(b)-(g). The principles. (d): no more than 30% of the investment capital in the companies of one group with mutual ownership.
@@q 2087 2107
@ref Dieu 99 (src:2087-2107)
GIVEN i IS AN `An investment position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 99(2): the investment complies with the principles` i MEANS
        i's `technical reserves are invested only in Vietnam`
    AND (NOT i's `the investment is funded by borrowing, or entrusted to invest in securities, real estate or equity in other enterprises`)
    AND i's `amount invested in companies of one group with mutual ownership, other than deposits at credit institutions and establishing an enterprise or a branch abroad` AT MOST i's `total investment capital` TIMES 30%
    AND (NOT i's `reinvested in shareholders, members or their related persons, other than deposits at a credit institution that is a shareholder or member`)
    AND (NOT i's `bought corporate bonds issued to restructure the issuer's own debts`)
    AND ((NOT i's `is entrusted investment`) OR i's `entrusted investment is with a licensed trustee for that line`)

-- Dieu 99(3) (in force from 1 January 2028): four investments an insurer may not make, with exceptions. Real estate
-- taken on foreclosure or set-off may be held for 3 years from the day it was taken.
@@q 2108 2125
@ref Dieu 99 (src:2108-2125)
GIVEN i IS AN `An investment position`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 99(3): the investment is a prohibited investment` i `the day in question` MEANS
    IF NOT `Dieu 156(2): the provision is in force on the day` `Dieu 99(3) and (4)` `the day in question`
    THEN REFUSE "Dieu 99(3) and (4) are not yet in force on that day (Dieu 156(2)); the provision of the old Law that governs until then is not among the sources"
    ELSE     i's `is real estate business outside the exceptions`
          OR (i's `is real estate held after foreclosure or set-off of debts` AND i's `years real estate has been held after foreclosure or set-off` ABOVE 3)
          OR i's `is precious metals or stones`
          OR i's `is intangible fixed assets not serving the insurance business`
          OR i's `is derivatives other than listed hedging derivatives`

@@q 2128 2132
@ref Dieu 99 (src:2128-2132)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 99(4)-(5): the Minister of Finance's rules on valuing investment assets and the Government's investment limits` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 99(4) delegates the valuation of investment assets to the Minister of Finance and Dieu 99(5) the investment limits to the Government; neither is among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 100: investing abroad`

-- Dieu 100(1)-(4). An insurer or reinsurer may invest abroad in two forms, from two sources, and on six conditions
-- including the Ministry's prior written approval; a foreign branch may not invest abroad.
@@q 2134 2169
@ref Dieu 100 (src:2134-2169)
GIVEN a IS AN `An investment abroad`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 100: the investment abroad is permitted` a MEANS
        (NOT a's `the investor is a foreign branch in Vietnam`)
    AND (a's `is establishing, funding or buying an insurer or reinsurer abroad, or a branch, representative office or other presence abroad` OR a's `is buying or selling securities or investing through funds or intermediaries abroad as the Government provides`)
    AND (a's `is funded from equity left after capital adequacy and solvency` OR a's `is funded from idle technical reserves of contracts linked to foreign investment indices or made with persons abroad`)
    AND a's `keeps the capital adequacy ratio and solvency`
    AND a's `complies with the insurance, investment and foreign exchange laws`
    AND a's `is made in the name of the insurer or reinsurer`
    AND a's `is managed and tracked separately`
    AND (NOT a's `covers a loss of the investment with money or assets of domestic policyholders`)
    AND a's `the Ministry of Finance approved in writing before the investment`

@@q 2170 2172
@ref Dieu 100 (src:2170-2172)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 100(5): the Government's conditions, limits and procedure for investing abroad` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 100(5) delegates the conditions, limits, dossier and procedure to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 101: separating owners' equity from premium sources, distributing surplus`

-- Dieu 101. V1: every insurer registers the principle with the Ministry of Finance and keeps three kinds of
-- separate records; a life insurer also separates its participating contracts by an approved method. From V2
-- (Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(8)): no registration for the first paragraph; a life insurer registers and keeps to the
-- approved method for the principles of separation and of surplus distribution on participating contracts; a non-life
-- insurer or foreign non-life branch notifies the principle in writing beforehand and keeps to what it notified.
-- The second paragraph names no duty for a reinsurer or a mutual organisation (fork F25).
@@q 2175 2192
@@qa 188 220
@ref Dieu 101 (src:2175-2192; src:law139-2025-qh15:188-220)
GIVEN s IS A `A separation of sources`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 101: the insurer meets the requirements on separating sources` s MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
           THEN     s's `separates and tracks owners' equity, premium sources and their assets`
                AND s's `separates and tracks revenue, cost and result of insurance business and investment`
                AND s's `separates and tracks premium and reserves inside and outside the territory`
                AND (CONSIDER s's `kind of insurer`
                     WHEN `a life insurer` THEN s's `registered the principles and the method approved by the Ministry for separating sources and distributing surplus` AND s's `follows the registered or notified principles`
                     WHEN `a non-life insurer` THEN s's `notified the principle of separation to the Ministry in writing before applying it` AND s's `follows the registered or notified principles`
                     WHEN `a branch of a foreign non-life insurer` THEN s's `notified the principle of separation to the Ministry in writing before applying it` AND s's `follows the registered or notified principles`
                     OTHERWISE TRUE)
           IF `the rules in force are those of V1 or later`
           THEN     s's `registered the principle with the Ministry of Finance`
                AND s's `separates and tracks owners' equity, premium sources and their assets`
                AND s's `separates and tracks revenue, cost and result of insurance business and investment`
                AND s's `separates and tracks premium and reserves inside and outside the territory`
                AND ((NOT (s's `kind of insurer` EQUALS `a life insurer` AND s's `has a participating life contract portfolio`)) OR s's `separates the participating portfolio by a method the Ministry approved`)
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "Law 08/2022/QH15 was not in force before 1 January 2023"

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 101: the Government's and the Minister of Finance's rules on registering, notifying and separating` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 101 delegates the dossier and procedure to the Government and the separation and the surplus principles to the Minister of Finance; neither is among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 102, 103, 104 and 108`

@@q 2197 2201
@ref Dieu 102 (src:2197-2201)
`Dieu 102 — the financial regime follows this Law and other laws; the Government details it (cross-reference and delegation; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "Financial regime: this Law and the other law; detail by the Government."

-- Dieu 103. The financial year is the calendar year; the first runs from the day the licence is granted to the last day of that year.
@@q 2203 2208
@ref Dieu 103 (src:2203-2208)
GIVEN y IS A `A financial year`
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 103: the first day of the financial year asked about` y MEANS
    IF y's `calendar year asked about` EQUALS DATE_YEAR (y's `date the licence was granted`)
    THEN y's `date the licence was granted`
    ELSE YMD (y's `calendar year asked about`) 1 1

GIVEN y IS A `A financial year`
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 103: the last day of the financial year asked about` y MEANS
    YMD (y's `calendar year asked about`) 12 31

@@q 2210 2212
@ref Dieu 104 (src:2210-2212)
`Dieu 104 — the accounting regime follows the law on accounting (cross-reference to another law; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "The law on accounting applies."

@@q 2273 2282
@ref Dieu 108 (src:2273-2282)
`Dieu 108 — financial governance: financial autonomy and answerability; strategy, procedures and structure to manage financial activity (a statement of duties without a testable fact beyond the assertion of compliance; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "The insurer is financially autonomous and builds the means to manage and supervise its finances."

§§ `Dieu 105: independent audit`

@@q 2214 2238
@ref Dieu 105 (src:2214-2238)
GIVEN r IS A `The audits and reports of an insurer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 105(1)-(2): the insurer has obtained the independent audit and confirmations` r MEANS
        r's `the annual financial statements were audited independently`
    AND r's `the solvency and risk management report was confirmed by an independent auditor`
    AND r's `the report on separating equity and premium sources was confirmed by an independent auditor`
    AND r's `the reports on linked funds and pension funds were confirmed by an independent auditor`

@@q 2233 2237
@ref Dieu 105 (src:2233-2237)
GIVEN r IS A `The audits and reports of an insurer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 105(3)(d): the auditor failed to notify the Ministry of Finance` r MEANS
    r's `the auditor found a material breach, fraud or unusual transaction` AND (NOT r's `the auditor notified the Ministry of Finance in writing`)

@@q 2239 2239
@ref Dieu 105 (src:2239)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 105(4): the Minister of Finance's rules on confirmations` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 105(4) delegates the detail of the confirmations to the Minister of Finance; the Minister's circular is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 106: reports`

@@q 2241 2252
@ref Dieu 106 (src:2241-2252)
GIVEN r IS A `The audits and reports of an insurer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 106(1): the insurer has sent the Ministry of Finance the periodic reports` r MEANS
        r's `sent the financial statements, and the cause and state if the audit opinion was not unqualified`
    AND r's `sent the report on insurance operations`
    AND r's `sent the report on separating equity and premium sources`
    AND r's `sent the solvency and risk management report`
    AND r's `sent the report on changes in capital for each risk`

@@q 2253 2258
@ref Dieu 106 (src:2253-2258)
GIVEN r IS A `The audits and reports of an insurer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 106(2): the insurer failed to report an unusual development or a failure to meet requirements` r MEANS
    r's `an unusual development affected solvency or reputation, or a financial or other requirement was not met` AND (NOT r's `reported that development to the Ministry of Finance`)

@@q 2259 2260
@ref Dieu 106 (src:2259-2260)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 106(3): the Minister of Finance's rules on reports and information` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 106(3) delegates the detail of reporting to the Minister of Finance; the Minister's circular is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 107: transferring profit and assets abroad`

@@q 2262 2271
@ref Dieu 107 (src:2262-2271)
GIVEN t IS A `A transfer of profit or assets abroad`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 107: the transfer abroad is permitted` t MEANS
        t's `follows Vietnamese law on transferring money and assets`
    AND (t's `is profit belonging to foreign investors left after setting aside funds, meeting financial obligations and keeping the capital adequacy ratio and solvency` OR t's `is assets belonging to foreign investors left after ending business in Vietnam`)
